<h2><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_L1Z1X_Mindnet#Leaders:~:text=I48S">I48S</a> <sub>(Agent)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The infantry must be in the system when it is activated for it to be eligible to be replaced. It cannot be replaced if it is moved into or produced in the active system later in the turn.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>If a player wishes to place a mech, but there are none left in their reinforcements, they may remove a mech from any system that does not contain one of their command tokens and place that instead. The mech will be placed undamaged.<sup>1,4</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_L1Z1X_Mindnet#Leaders:~:text=2RAM">2RAM</a> <sub>(Commander)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Those units still have <a href="/R_planetary_shield"><sc>Planetary Shield</sc></a>. The player that owns those units may still use the ability of the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Warfare_Technologies#Magen_Defense_Grid"><i>Magen Defense Grid</i></a> technology.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_L1Z1X_Mindnet#Leaders:~:text=The%20Helmsman">The Helmsman</a> &mdash; <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_L1Z1X_Mindnet#Leaders:~:text=Dark%20Space%20Navigation">Dark Space Navigation</a> <sub>(Hero)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Ships in systems with one of the L1Z1X player&rsquo;s command tokens may move.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>A future rule change will allow a player&rsquo;s ships to transport units from systems that contain that player&rsquo;s command token when those ships move outside of a tactical action.<sup>4</sup></li>
    <li>Ships move directly to their destination system. They may only transport units from their origin system.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>Ships moving out of a gravity rift must roll for removal.<sup>1,2,3,4</sup></li>
    <li>Ships cannot move into a supernova, even if it contains one of the L1Z1X player&rsquo;s command tokens.<sup>1,2,3</sup></li>
    <ol><li>Ships may travel into an asteroid field only if the L1Z1X player owns the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Propulsion_Technologies#Antimass_Deflectors"><i>Antimass Deflectors</i></a> technology.<sup>2</sup></li></ol>
    <li><i>Dark Space Navigation</i> may be used to move ships into the wormhole nexus. If the nexus is inactive, this will cause it to activate.<sup>1,8</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_L1Z1X_Mindnet#Mech:~:text=Annihilator">Annihilator</a> <sub>(Mech)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>An Annihilator may bombard when using the L1Z1X player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_L1Z1X_Mindnet#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Harrow"><sc>Harrow</sc></a> ability if that mech is not currently participating in ground combat, even if it has been committed to a different planet, and has been or will be involved in another ground combat during the current invasion.<sup>2</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_L1Z1X_Mindnet#Breakthrough:~:text=Fealty%20Uplink">Fealty Uplink</a> <sub>(Breakthrough)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If the L1Z1X player gains control of an uncontrolled planet, they may choose if they place the infantry before or after they explore the planet.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>The L1Z1X player must mandatorily place the infantry.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>
</article>
